#====================================================================
# E550.kv - Windows Conan cross-build and HMDFS signed ELF execution
#====================================================================

id:                     E550
draft:                  true
trigger_tool:           conan|make|ssh|binary-sign-tool
phase:                  build|packaging|w3
error_signature:        export CC=.*not recognized|
                         make: No rule to make target|
                         clang: error: no such file or directory: .*sysroot|
                         Permission denied.*ELF|
                         binary-sign-tool.*self-sign
severity:               2
category:               conan, cross-build, windows-shell, hmdfs, signing
match_keywords:         basic_layout, source_folder, build_folder, make, CC,
                         tools.build:compiler_executables, tools.build:sysroot,
                         tools.build:cflags, strftime %F, SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH,
                         UID drift, shared storage, owner execute, group execute,
                         binary-sign-tool, selfSign=1, display-sign

root_cause:             Windows Conan package builds invoke commands through
                         cmd.exe while upstream Makefiles assume a POSIX shell;
                         basic_layout also separates source_folder from
                         build_folder.  If the recipe leaves CC/CFLAGS to an
                         unbound shell, the host compiler is selected or paths
                         containing spaces are split.  On HarmonyOS shared
                         storage, SSH sessions can expose a different numeric
                         UID from the file owner; a signed ELF with only owner
                         or group execute bits can then fail before platform
                         signature validation.
affected_scope:         C/C++ Conan recipes using Make/autotools on a Windows
                         host for OHOS targets, and any W3 flow staging ELFs in
                         HMDFS or another shared UID-mapped directory.
verification_cmd:       conan create <recipe> --profile:host <ohos> --profile:build <windows>;
                         test -x <target>; binary-sign-tool display-sign -inFile <target>;
                         sha256sum <target>; run the registered upstream check
                         entry in a POSIX-compatible shell; perform exact-byte
                         transfer/readback and one target launch.
rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:            Bind source_folder for source Makefiles.  For OHOS
                         cross builds, read compiler_executables/cflags/sysroot
                         from Conan conf and invoke the compiler with an
                         argument-list-safe command; keep host generators
                         separate.  Before W3 launch, transfer the official
                         native signer, self-sign a task-private copy, verify
                         display-sign and executable mode, and retain group or
                         owner execute bits across UID drift.
rec_description:        Do not use POSIX export in self.run on Windows; do not
                         treat a successful chmod or host JAR signature as
                         target acceptance.  Freeze payload hashes, endpoint,
                         boot_id, UID, signer and launch command before the
                         only launch.  If launch is consumed, record the
                         terminal failure and create a new successor.
rec_command:             Use self.run(command_line, cwd=self.source_folder)
                         with subprocess.list2cmdline on Windows; use
                         binary-sign-tool sign -selfSign 1 followed by
                         display-sign, then exact status/output readback.
rec_auto_fix:            false
fallback_priority:       2
fallback_approach:       Run upstream shell checks in a POSIX-compatible host
                         only when the target recipe and test inventory remain
                         unchanged; label host libc shims as validation-only.
fallback_description:    A host test pass cannot replace target ELF signing,
                         HMDFS execution or a fresh W3 transaction.
fallback_auto_fix:       false
principles:              P004, P006, P009
caused_by:               []
similar_to:              [E550]
doc_file:                doc/E550.md
evidence:                F:\\HarmonyPC\\scdoc-1.11.3-20260904\\conan-create-scdoc.log;
                         F:\\HarmonyPC\\scdoc-1.11.3-20260904\\upstream-tests-final.log;
                         F:\\HarmonyPC\\scdoc-1.11.3-20260904\\w3-r001\\transaction.json;
                         F:\\HarmonyPC\\scdoc-1.11.3-20260904\\w3-r002\\transaction.json
